# .platform/ is read-only

In a Yes Human pack, `.platform/` is a fresh clone of the platform made by `.cursor/install.sh`. It is not part of this repo and is replaced on every install.

- Do not commit, push, or open PRs from `.platform/`.
- The pack's `.cursor/*` files are managed by Yes Human. Do not rewrite them (install script, environment, Dockerfile, rules, or skills). If install fails or you are tempted to change `.cursor/*`, file an `agent-feedback` issue on the pack (see its `AGENTS.md`) and stop.
- Pack `.cursor/skills` holds the Yes Human pack plugin skills (`yeshuman-pack-orientation`, `yeshuman-pack-feature`, `yeshuman-platform-request`, `yeshuman-linear-evidence`) plus skills Yes Human has explicitly approved for packs (currently `plan-to-make-a-plan`). Use the fully qualified `yeshuman-*` names; never shorten to `yh-*`.
- Do not copy or add any other platform skill into a pack's `.cursor/skills` — not `create-domain-slice`, not `create-django-app`, not anything else from `.platform/.cursor/skills` unless Yes Human approved it. Those live in the platform repo. Read them from `.platform/` if you need them; do not land them in this pack.
- Change this pack (config, theme, seeds, `plugin/`) when the platform's extension points allow it.
- When a request needs a platform change, you may prototype in `.platform/` to prove it, then file a `platform-request` issue on this pack with the diff. See the `yeshuman-platform-request` skill.
